\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Angels holy,
\par High and lowly,
\par Sing the praises of the Lord
\par Earth and sky; all living nature;
\par Man, the stamp of thy Creator,
\par Praise ye praise ye God the Lord
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sun and moon bright,
\par Night and noon-light,
\par Starry temples azure-floored;
\par Cloud and rain, and wild wind's madness,
\par Sons of God that shout for gladness,
\par Praise ye praise ye God the Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Ocean hoary,
\par Tell His glory;
\par Cliffs, where tumbling seas have roared,
\par Pulse of waters, blithely beating,
\par Wave advancing, wave retreating,
\par Praise ye praise ye God the Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Rock and highland,
\par Wood and island,
\par Crag, where eagle's pride hath soared;
\par Mighty mountains, purple-breasted,
\par Peaks cloud-cleaving, snowy-crested,
\par Praise ye praise ye God the Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Rolling river,
\par Praise Him ever,
\par From the mountains deep vein poured;
\par Silver fountain, clearly gushing,
\par Troubled torrent, madly rushing,
\par Praise ye praise ye God the Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Praise Him ever,
\par Bounteous giver,
\par Praise Him, Father, Friend and Lord
\par Each glad soul its free course winging,
\par Each glad voice its free song singing,
\par Praise the great and mighty Lord.
\par                                         Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

